  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44115650",
      "title": "A Closer Look At Dynamic Inline Style Binding",
      "lectureOrder": 121,
      "videoOrder": 115,
      "sourceHash": "63c0d9a42f3cee1e8968ff2e32bd2c40d43e56d3d0f86ee2bc8063cd7354704c",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.66,
          "end": 2.7,
          "en": "So this is another version",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.7,
          "end": 5.25,
          "en": "of this class binding syntax,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.25,
          "end": 8.94,
          "en": "which you should be aware of when working with Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.94,
          "end": 10.72,
          "en": "It's also worth knowing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.692,
          "end": 15.443,
          "en": "that besides binding classes dynamically in Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.443,
          "end": 20.25,
          "en": "you can actually also bind styles dynamically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.25,
          "end": 24.12,
          "en": "So if you directly wanna set a certain style.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.12,
          "end": 27.66,
          "en": "And you can do this again with square brackets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.66,
          "end": 31.901,
          "en": "and then the style keyword, the style property name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.901,
          "end": 35.817,
          "en": "and then you can again, just as with class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.817,
          "end": 40.817,
          "en": "either pass in an object where you target different styles,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 41.08,
          "end": 44.389,
          "en": "like for example, font size.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 44.389,
          "end": 48.78,
          "en": "I'm using the string version since I have a dash in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 48.78,
          "end": 51.9,
          "en": "And you could then set this to a hardcoded value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 51.9,
          "end": 54.06,
          "en": "like 64 pixels",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 54.06,
          "end": 57.63,
          "en": "or to the result of some TypeScript expression",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 57.63,
          "end": 59.553,
          "en": "that produces that value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 60.524,
          "end": 64.41,
          "en": "If you save that, you see the text much bigger.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 64.41,
          "end": 67.17,
          "en": "Besides defining this property like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 67.17,
          "end": 70.74,
          "en": "you could also use this camel case notation here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 70.74,
          "end": 74.7,
          "en": "This is an alternative you can use here for these styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 74.7,
          "end": 78.18,
          "en": "if you're targeting a style that consists of multiple words",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 78.18,
          "end": 80.193,
          "en": "that are separated by dashes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 81.06,
          "end": 83.25,
          "en": "Since dashes aren't allowed here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 83.25,
          "end": 86.73,
          "en": "you either have to wrap this with quotes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 86.73,
          "end": 90.617,
          "en": "or as an alternative, use this camel case notation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 90.617,
          "end": 92.793,
          "en": "The result will be the same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 93.989,
          "end": 97.38,
          "en": "Now, if you're only targeting one single style,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 97.38,
          "end": 99.78,
          "en": "you can also use a shorter notation here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 99.78,
          "end": 101.78999999999999,
          "en": "just as you could with class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 101.78999999999999,
          "end": 105.384,
          "en": "and use style dot font size in this example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 105.384,
          "end": 108.42,
          "en": "and then directly set the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 108.42,
          "end": 110.67,
          "en": "to which this style should be set.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 110.67,
          "end": 112.11,
          "en": "Again, this here, however,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 112.11,
          "end": 115.8,
          "en": "is some dynamically evaluated expression.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 115.8,
          "end": 118.32,
          "en": "So if you want to have a hardcoded string here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 118.32,
          "end": 120.273,
          "en": "you must wrap it with quotes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 121.23,
          "end": 122.82,
          "en": "Otherwise it will be treated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 122.82,
          "end": 124.95,
          "en": "and executed as TypeScript code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 124.95,
          "end": 128.07,
          "en": "and this is not valid TypeScript code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 128.07,
          "end": 130.233,
          "en": "so the single quotes are needed here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 131.1,
          "end": 133.443,
          "en": "With that, I still have that big text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 134.52,
          "end": 137.49,
          "en": "Now here, I don't need to target any styles,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 137.49,
          "end": 140.49,
          "en": "so I'll get rid of that, but you should know about that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 140.49,
          "end": 144.24,
          "en": "just as you should know about this class binding feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 144.24,
          "end": 147.42000000000002,
          "en": "By the way, one place where you can see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 147.42000000000002,
          "end": 151.23,
          "en": "that style binding feature in action already",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 151.23,
          "end": 155.1,
          "en": "in this application here is in a traffic component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 155.1,
          "end": 156.469,
          "en": "HTML file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 156.469,
          "end": 161.16,
          "en": "In there I am using Angular's style binding feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 161.16,
          "end": 166.16,
          "en": "to dynamically set the height style of that div",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 166.563,
          "end": 171.563,
          "en": "to a calculated value where I take the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 172.2,
          "end": 173.79,
          "en": "of one of these data points",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 173.79,
          "end": 177.66,
          "en": "and divide that by the highest possible value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 177.66,
          "end": 181.11,
          "en": "multiply it with 100 to get a percentage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 181.11,
          "end": 182.963,
          "en": "between 0 and 100,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 182.963,
          "end": 185.97,
          "en": "and concatenate that to a string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 185.97,
          "end": 188.58,
          "en": "with the percentage sign at the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 188.58,
          "end": 192.471,
          "en": "so that the height style property of this div is set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 192.471,
          "end": 196.904,
          "en": "to some percentage between 0 and 100.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 196.904,
          "end": 200.43,
          "en": "And that was already part of the starting project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 200.43,
          "end": 204.03,
          "en": "in case you wondered what this syntax was all about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 204.03,
          "end": 208.953,
          "en": "Well, now you know that is Angular's style binding syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
